title: Claude Code
id: claude-code-adapter
order: 11
description: "Use Claude Code as a chat backend in TanStack AI — agent harness with local tool execution, stateful coding sessions, and tool bridging via @tanstack/ai-claude-code."
keywords:
  - tanstack ai
  - claude code
  - claude agent sdk
  - anthropic
  - harness
  - agent
  - coding agent
  - adapter
---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Claude Code adapter runs "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (via the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk"},{"type":"text","value":") as a chat backend. Unlike HTTP provider adapters, this is a "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"harness adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": Claude Code runs its own agent loop and executes its own tools — bash, file reads and edits, glob/grep search, web search — locally on your server. Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" call runs one full harness turn; the harness's tool activity streams back as already-resolved tool-call events your UI can render."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-only."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The harness spawns the Claude Code runtime as a subprocess, so this adapter only works in a Node.js server environment — never in the browser. Treat it like giving Claude a shell on the machine it runs on, and configure permissions accordingly."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A runnable demo lives at "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-cloudflare","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/sandbox-cloudflare"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — pick Claude Code, Codex, or Grok Build in the UI, with session resume, the harness tool timeline, and tool bridging, wired into a TanStack Start app on Workers. For the same wiring on plain Node with durable, refresh-surviving runs (this adapter on Docker), see "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-web","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/sandbox-web"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"authentication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Authentication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your laptop can already have "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":". A CI runner only has\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". The default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":". Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":"\nwhen you want "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"\n\nclaudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\")\nclaudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", { authMode: \"host\" })","lang":"ts"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default): inject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" (or pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":": use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not inject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", {\n    cwd: \"/path/to/project\",\n    permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Fix the failing test in utils.test.ts\" }],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuration"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cwd"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working directory for the harness session. Defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"process.cwd()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code permission mode ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'default'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'acceptEdits'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'bypassPermissions'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'plan'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'dontAsk'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'auto'"},{"type":"text","value":"). See the permissions note below."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowedTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in tools the harness may use without prompting (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['Read', 'Grep', 'Bash(npm test:*)']"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"disallowedTools"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in tools removed from the harness entirely."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTurns"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maximum harness-internal turns per run."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPromptMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'append'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) keeps Claude Code's preset system prompt and appends your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"systemPrompts"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'replace'"},{"type":"text","value":" sends yours as the entire prompt."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcpServers"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra MCP servers passed through to the harness untouched."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authMode"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'api-key'"},{"type":"text","value":" (default) injects "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'host'"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":". Also valid on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":". See "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"apiKey"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic API key for the harness subprocess."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"env"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra environment variables for the harness subprocess."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pathToClaudeCodeExecutable"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a specific Claude Code executable instead of the SDK's bundled one."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"streamPartials"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Emit true token-level deltas for text and tool-call arguments (default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"). When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":", both emit whole from the complete message."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canUseTool"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom permission handler; replaces the adapter's default handler."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"settingSources"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code settings tiers to load. Default "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['project']"},{"type":"text","value":": the workspace's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLAUDE.md"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude/skills"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".mcp.json"},{"type":"text","value":" apply, and the host's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~/.claude"},{"type":"text","value":" (plugins, hooks, skills) is not loaded. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"['user', 'project', 'local']"},{"type":"text","value":" for CLI-equivalent behavior, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[]"},{"type":"text","value":" to load no settings."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Permissions on headless servers."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Without an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canUseTool"},{"type":"text","value":", the adapter installs a safe default handler: bridged TanStack tools always run, and any built-in tool call that would normally prompt a human is denied with guidance instead of hanging the request. To let the harness edit files or run commands, set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"permissionMode: 'acceptEdits'"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'bypassPermissions'"},{"type":"text","value":", or enumerate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"allowedTools"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"stateful-sessions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stateful Sessions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Claude Code sessions are stateful — the harness keeps the full working context (files read, commands run, conclusions reached) between turns. The adapter surfaces the session id of every run as a custom stream event named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-code.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":"; thread it back via "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions.sessionId"},{"type":"text","value":" to resume the session. When resuming, only the latest user message is sent — the harness already holds the prior context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude-code.session-id"},{"type":"text","value":" event payload also includes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":", an array of skills loaded during SDK initialization (or an empty array when none are reported)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server endpoint:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  // Extra fields the client puts in the connection `body` arrive here.\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === \"string\"\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined;\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", {\n      cwd: \"/path/to/project\",\n      permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\",\n    }),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client (React) — capture the session id from the custom event and send it back on subsequent requests:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nfunction CodingAssistant() {\n  const [sessionId, setSessionId] = useState<string | undefined>(undefined);\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\", () => ({\n      body: { sessionId },\n    })),\n    onCustomEvent: (name, value) => {\n      if (\n        name === \"claude-code.session-id\" &&\n        typeof value === \"object\" &&\n        value !== null &&\n        \"sessionId\" in value &&\n        typeof value.sessionId === \"string\"\n      ) {\n        setSessionId(value.sessionId);\n      }\n    },\n  });\n\n  // ... render messages; harness tool activity (Bash, Edit, Read, ...)\n  // arrives as regular tool-call parts with their results attached.\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sessions are stored on the machine that ran them ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~/.claude/projects/"},{"type":"text","value":"), so resuming only works on the same server instance. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions: { forkSession: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" alongside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionId"},{"type":"text","value":" to branch a session instead of continuing it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tools","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tools"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two kinds of tools flow through this adapter:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"loose":true,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in harness tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Bash"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Read"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Write"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Edit"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Glob"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Grep"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"WebSearch"},{"type":"text","value":", ...) are executed by Claude Code itself. Their activity streams back as tool-call events with results already attached, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" UIs render them with no extra wiring — but your code never executes them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your TanStack tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are bridged "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"into"}]},{"type":"text","value":" the harness as an in-process MCP server. Define them as usual with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition().server()"},{"type":"text","value":"; the model sees them as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mcp__tanstack__<name>"},{"type":"text","value":" and the adapter strips the prefix on the way back out, so events match the names you registered."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { chat, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nconst lookupTicket = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"lookup_ticket\",\n  description: \"Look up an issue ticket by id\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ ticketId: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ ticketId }) => {\n  return { ticketId, status: \"open\", title: \"Crash on startup\" };\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's the status of ticket T-123?\" }],\n  tools: [lookupTicket],\n});","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client-side and approval-gated tools are not supported."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The harness executes tools inside a live subprocess, which cannot pause across HTTP requests to wait for a browser round-trip or a human approval. Passing a tool without a server "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execute()"},{"type":"text","value":" implementation — or one marked "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"needsApproval"},{"type":"text","value":" — fails fast with a descriptive error. Run those tools outside the harness with a regular provider adapter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"structured-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structured Output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":". Claude Code runs one harness turn, uses its native tools, and returns a typed object. The schema JSON is passed to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json-schema"},{"type":"text","value":" as inline JSON (the CLI rejects a file path). Tool activity and prose stream as usual. The object arrives as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structured-output.complete"},{"type":"text","value":", including when Claude delivers it through its built-in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StructuredOutput"},{"type":"text","value":" tool."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the adapter loads only project settings ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--setting-sources project"},{"type":"text","value":"). Workspace projections (instructions, skills, MCP config) are project-scoped, so they apply. The host's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"~/.claude"},{"type":"text","value":" is not loaded, so a local-process run does not pick up your personal skills and hooks. A cloned repo's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude/settings.json"},{"type":"text","value":" and hooks apply to the run. Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"settingSources"},{"type":"text","value":" to change this. The adapter does not pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--bare"},{"type":"text","value":", because that flag ignores a host "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On local-process, Claude uses your host "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"claude login"},{"type":"text","value":". On Docker, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ANTHROPIC_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" in the process env. A container has no host login."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"\nimport { defineSandbox, withSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n})\n\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Review this repo.\" }],\n  outputSchema: Report,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n\nreport.summary","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the client, pass the same schema to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" and read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"final"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"partial"},{"type":"text","value":" stays empty until the end."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nfunction ReportView() {\n  const { final, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: Report,\n  })\n\n  if (isLoading) return <p>The agent is inspecting the repo.</p>\n  if (!final) return null\n  return <p>{final.summary}</p>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you only need to extract JSON from a prompt and do not need a sandbox, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-anthropic"},{"type":"text","value":". That path is faster."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Full walkthrough, including the client: "},{"type":"link","href":"../structured-outputs/harnesses","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Harness Agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server-only (Node)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The harness spawns a subprocess; Windows support is untested."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The harness owns the agent loop."}]},{"type":"text","value":" TanStack's agent-loop strategies and per-iteration middleware don't apply inside a harness turn; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maxTurns"},{"type":"text","value":" is the equivalent control."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No sampling controls."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"temperature"},{"type":"text","value":"-style options don't exist here."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sessions are machine-local."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Resume requires hitting the same server instance."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cold starts."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Each call spawns a harness turn; expect higher first-token latency than HTTP adapters."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"authentication","text":"Authentication","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"configuration","text":"Configuration","level":2},{"id":"stateful-sessions","text":"Stateful Sessions","level":2},{"id":"tools","text":"Tools","level":2},{"id":"structured-output","text":"Structured Output","level":2},{"id":"limitations","text":"Limitations","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe Claude Code adapter runs [Claude Code](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code) (via the `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) as a chat backend. Unlike HTTP provider adapters, this is a **harness adapter**: Claude Code runs its own agent loop and executes its own tools — bash, file reads and edits, glob/grep search, web search — locally on your server. Each `chat()` call runs one full harness turn; the harness's tool activity streams back as already-resolved tool-call events your UI can render.\n\n> **Server-only.** The harness spawns the Claude Code runtime as a subprocess, so this adapter only works in a Node.js server environment — never in the browser. Treat it like giving Claude a shell on the machine it runs on, and configure permissions accordingly.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nvue: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\npreact: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nangular: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\noctane: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nA runnable demo lives at [`examples/sandbox-cloudflare`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-cloudflare) — pick Claude Code, Codex, or Grok Build in the UI, with session resume, the harness tool timeline, and tool bridging, wired into a TanStack Start app on Workers. For the same wiring on plain Node with durable, refresh-surviving runs (this adapter on Docker), see [`examples/sandbox-web`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-web).\n\n## Authentication\n\nYour laptop can already have `claude login`. A CI runner only has\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. The default `authMode` is `'api-key'`. Set `'host'`\nwhen you want `claude login`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"\n\nclaudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\")\nclaudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", { authMode: \"host\" })\n```\n\n- `'api-key'` (default): inject `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (or pass `apiKey`).\n- `'host'`: use `claude login`. Do not inject `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", {\n    cwd: \"/path/to/project\",\n    permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Fix the failing test in utils.test.ts\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Option                       | Description                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cwd`                        | Working directory for the harness session. Defaults to `process.cwd()`.                                                                            |\n| `permissionMode`             | Claude Code permission mode (`'default'`, `'acceptEdits'`, `'bypassPermissions'`, `'plan'`, `'dontAsk'`, `'auto'`). See the permissions note below. |\n| `allowedTools`               | Built-in tools the harness may use without prompting (e.g. `['Read', 'Grep', 'Bash(npm test:*)']`).                                                |\n| `disallowedTools`            | Built-in tools removed from the harness entirely.                                                                                                  |\n| `maxTurns`                   | Maximum harness-internal turns per run.                                                                                                            |\n| `systemPromptMode`           | `'append'` (default) keeps Claude Code's preset system prompt and appends your `systemPrompts`; `'replace'` sends yours as the entire prompt.       |\n| `mcpServers`                 | Extra MCP servers passed through to the harness untouched.                                                                                         |\n| `authMode`                   | `'api-key'` (default) injects `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. `'host'` uses `claude login`. Also valid on `modelOptions`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth). |\n| `apiKey`                     | Anthropic API key for the harness subprocess.                                                                                                       |\n| `env`                        | Extra environment variables for the harness subprocess.                                                                                            |\n| `pathToClaudeCodeExecutable` | Use a specific Claude Code executable instead of the SDK's bundled one.                                                                             |\n| `streamPartials`             | Emit true token-level deltas for text and tool-call arguments (default `true`). When `false`, both emit whole from the complete message.            |\n| `canUseTool`                 | Custom permission handler; replaces the adapter's default handler.                                                                                  |\n| `settingSources`             | Claude Code settings tiers to load. Default `['project']`: the workspace's `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills`, and `.mcp.json` apply, and the host's `~/.claude` (plugins, hooks, skills) is not loaded. Pass `['user', 'project', 'local']` for CLI-equivalent behavior, or `[]` to load no settings. |\n\n**Permissions on headless servers.** Without an explicit `permissionMode` or `canUseTool`, the adapter installs a safe default handler: bridged TanStack tools always run, and any built-in tool call that would normally prompt a human is denied with guidance instead of hanging the request. To let the harness edit files or run commands, set `permissionMode: 'acceptEdits'` / `'bypassPermissions'`, or enumerate `allowedTools`.\n\n## Stateful Sessions\n\nClaude Code sessions are stateful — the harness keeps the full working context (files read, commands run, conclusions reached) between turns. The adapter surfaces the session id of every run as a custom stream event named `claude-code.session-id`; thread it back via `modelOptions.sessionId` to resume the session. When resuming, only the latest user message is sent — the harness already holds the prior context.\n\nThe `claude-code.session-id` event payload also includes `skills`, an array of skills loaded during SDK initialization (or an empty array when none are reported).\n\nServer endpoint:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  // Extra fields the client puts in the connection `body` arrive here.\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === \"string\"\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined;\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", {\n      cwd: \"/path/to/project\",\n      permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\",\n    }),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nClient (React) — capture the session id from the custom event and send it back on subsequent requests:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nfunction CodingAssistant() {\n  const [sessionId, setSessionId] = useState<string | undefined>(undefined);\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\", () => ({\n      body: { sessionId },\n    })),\n    onCustomEvent: (name, value) => {\n      if (\n        name === \"claude-code.session-id\" &&\n        typeof value === \"object\" &&\n        value !== null &&\n        \"sessionId\" in value &&\n        typeof value.sessionId === \"string\"\n      ) {\n        setSessionId(value.sessionId);\n      }\n    },\n  });\n\n  // ... render messages; harness tool activity (Bash, Edit, Read, ...)\n  // arrives as regular tool-call parts with their results attached.\n}\n```\n\nSessions are stored on the machine that ran them (`~/.claude/projects/`), so resuming only works on the same server instance. Pass `modelOptions: { forkSession: true }` alongside `sessionId` to branch a session instead of continuing it.\n\n## Tools\n\nTwo kinds of tools flow through this adapter:\n\n1. **Built-in harness tools** (`Bash`, `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Glob`, `Grep`, `WebSearch`, ...) are executed by Claude Code itself. Their activity streams back as tool-call events with results already attached, so `useChat` UIs render them with no extra wiring — but your code never executes them.\n\n2. **Your TanStack tools** are bridged *into* the harness as an in-process MCP server. Define them as usual with `toolDefinition().server()`; the model sees them as `mcp__tanstack__<name>` and the adapter strips the prefix on the way back out, so events match the names you registered.\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { chat, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nconst lookupTicket = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"lookup_ticket\",\n  description: \"Look up an issue ticket by id\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ ticketId: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ ticketId }) => {\n  return { ticketId, status: \"open\", title: \"Crash on startup\" };\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's the status of ticket T-123?\" }],\n  tools: [lookupTicket],\n});\n```\n\n**Client-side and approval-gated tools are not supported.** The harness executes tools inside a live subprocess, which cannot pause across HTTP requests to wait for a browser round-trip or a human approval. Passing a tool without a server `execute()` implementation — or one marked `needsApproval` — fails fast with a descriptive error. Run those tools outside the harness with a regular provider adapter.\n\n## Structured Output\n\nPass `outputSchema` on `chat()`. Claude Code runs one harness turn, uses its native tools, and returns a typed object. The schema JSON is passed to `--json-schema` as inline JSON (the CLI rejects a file path). Tool activity and prose stream as usual. The object arrives as `structured-output.complete`, including when Claude delivers it through its built-in `StructuredOutput` tool.\n\nBy default, the adapter loads only project settings (`--setting-sources project`). Workspace projections (instructions, skills, MCP config) are project-scoped, so they apply. The host's `~/.claude` is not loaded, so a local-process run does not pick up your personal skills and hooks. A cloned repo's `.claude/settings.json` and hooks apply to the run. Set `settingSources` to change this. The adapter does not pass `--bare`, because that flag ignores a host `claude login`.\n\nOn local-process, Claude uses your host `claude login`. On Docker, pass `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the process env. A container has no host login.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"\nimport { defineSandbox, withSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n})\n\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Review this repo.\" }],\n  outputSchema: Report,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n\nreport.summary\n```\n\nOn the client, pass the same schema to `useChat` and read `final`. `partial` stays empty until the end.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nfunction ReportView() {\n  const { final, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: Report,\n  })\n\n  if (isLoading) return <p>The agent is inspecting the repo.</p>\n  if (!final) return null\n  return <p>{final.summary}</p>\n}\n```\n\nIf you only need to extract JSON from a prompt and do not need a sandbox, use `@tanstack/ai-anthropic`. That path is faster.\n\nFull walkthrough, including the client: [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Server-only (Node).** The harness spawns a subprocess; Windows support is untested.\n- **The harness owns the agent loop.** TanStack's agent-loop strategies and per-iteration middleware don't apply inside a harness turn; `maxTurns` is the equivalent control.\n- **No sampling controls.** `temperature`-style options don't exist here.\n- **Sessions are machine-local.** Resume requires hitting the same server instance.\n- **Cold starts.** Each call spawns a harness turn; expect higher first-token latency than HTTP adapters.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Claude Code\nid: claude-code-adapter\norder: 11\ndescription: \"Use Claude Code as a chat backend in TanStack AI — agent harness with local tool execution, stateful coding sessions, and tool bridging via @tanstack/ai-claude-code.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - claude code\n  - claude agent sdk\n  - anthropic\n  - harness\n  - agent\n  - coding agent\n  - adapter\n---\n\nThe Claude Code adapter runs [Claude Code](https://docs.anthropic.com/en/docs/claude-code) (via the `@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk`) as a chat backend. Unlike HTTP provider adapters, this is a **harness adapter**: Claude Code runs its own agent loop and executes its own tools — bash, file reads and edits, glob/grep search, web search — locally on your server. Each `chat()` call runs one full harness turn; the harness's tool activity streams back as already-resolved tool-call events your UI can render.\n\n> **Server-only.** The harness spawns the Claude Code runtime as a subprocess, so this adapter only works in a Node.js server environment — never in the browser. Treat it like giving Claude a shell on the machine it runs on, and configure permissions accordingly.\n\n## Installation\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nvue: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\npreact: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nangular: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\noctane: @tanstack/ai-claude-code\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nA runnable demo lives at [`examples/sandbox-cloudflare`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-cloudflare) — pick Claude Code, Codex, or Grok Build in the UI, with session resume, the harness tool timeline, and tool bridging, wired into a TanStack Start app on Workers. For the same wiring on plain Node with durable, refresh-surviving runs (this adapter on Docker), see [`examples/sandbox-web`](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/tree/main/examples/sandbox-web).\n\n## Authentication\n\nYour laptop can already have `claude login`. A CI runner only has\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. The default `authMode` is `'api-key'`. Set `'host'`\nwhen you want `claude login`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth).\n\n```ts\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"\n\nclaudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\")\nclaudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", { authMode: \"host\" })\n```\n\n- `'api-key'` (default): inject `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (or pass `apiKey`).\n- `'host'`: use `claude login`. Do not inject `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.\n\n## Basic Usage\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", {\n    cwd: \"/path/to/project\",\n    permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\",\n  }),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Fix the failing test in utils.test.ts\" }],\n});\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Option                       | Description                                                                                                                                       |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cwd`                        | Working directory for the harness session. Defaults to `process.cwd()`.                                                                            |\n| `permissionMode`             | Claude Code permission mode (`'default'`, `'acceptEdits'`, `'bypassPermissions'`, `'plan'`, `'dontAsk'`, `'auto'`). See the permissions note below. |\n| `allowedTools`               | Built-in tools the harness may use without prompting (e.g. `['Read', 'Grep', 'Bash(npm test:*)']`).                                                |\n| `disallowedTools`            | Built-in tools removed from the harness entirely.                                                                                                  |\n| `maxTurns`                   | Maximum harness-internal turns per run.                                                                                                            |\n| `systemPromptMode`           | `'append'` (default) keeps Claude Code's preset system prompt and appends your `systemPrompts`; `'replace'` sends yours as the entire prompt.       |\n| `mcpServers`                 | Extra MCP servers passed through to the harness untouched.                                                                                         |\n| `authMode`                   | `'api-key'` (default) injects `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`. `'host'` uses `claude login`. Also valid on `modelOptions`. See [Harness Auth](../sandbox/auth). |\n| `apiKey`                     | Anthropic API key for the harness subprocess.                                                                                                       |\n| `env`                        | Extra environment variables for the harness subprocess.                                                                                            |\n| `pathToClaudeCodeExecutable` | Use a specific Claude Code executable instead of the SDK's bundled one.                                                                             |\n| `streamPartials`             | Emit true token-level deltas for text and tool-call arguments (default `true`). When `false`, both emit whole from the complete message.            |\n| `canUseTool`                 | Custom permission handler; replaces the adapter's default handler.                                                                                  |\n| `settingSources`             | Claude Code settings tiers to load. Default `['project']`: the workspace's `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/skills`, and `.mcp.json` apply, and the host's `~/.claude` (plugins, hooks, skills) is not loaded. Pass `['user', 'project', 'local']` for CLI-equivalent behavior, or `[]` to load no settings. |\n\n**Permissions on headless servers.** Without an explicit `permissionMode` or `canUseTool`, the adapter installs a safe default handler: bridged TanStack tools always run, and any built-in tool call that would normally prompt a human is denied with guidance instead of hanging the request. To let the harness edit files or run commands, set `permissionMode: 'acceptEdits'` / `'bypassPermissions'`, or enumerate `allowedTools`.\n\n## Stateful Sessions\n\nClaude Code sessions are stateful — the harness keeps the full working context (files read, commands run, conclusions reached) between turns. The adapter surfaces the session id of every run as a custom stream event named `claude-code.session-id`; thread it back via `modelOptions.sessionId` to resume the session. When resuming, only the latest user message is sent — the harness already holds the prior context.\n\nThe `claude-code.session-id` event payload also includes `skills`, an array of skills loaded during SDK initialization (or an empty array when none are reported).\n\nServer endpoint:\n\n```typescript\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request);\n\n  // Extra fields the client puts in the connection `body` arrive here.\n  const sessionId =\n    typeof params.forwardedProps.sessionId === \"string\"\n      ? params.forwardedProps.sessionId\n      : undefined;\n\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\", {\n      cwd: \"/path/to/project\",\n      permissionMode: \"acceptEdits\",\n    }),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    modelOptions: { sessionId },\n  });\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream);\n}\n```\n\nClient (React) — capture the session id from the custom event and send it back on subsequent requests:\n\n```typescript\nimport { useState } from \"react\";\nimport { useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\";\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from \"@tanstack/ai-client\";\n\nfunction CodingAssistant() {\n  const [sessionId, setSessionId] = useState<string | undefined>(undefined);\n\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/chat\", () => ({\n      body: { sessionId },\n    })),\n    onCustomEvent: (name, value) => {\n      if (\n        name === \"claude-code.session-id\" &&\n        typeof value === \"object\" &&\n        value !== null &&\n        \"sessionId\" in value &&\n        typeof value.sessionId === \"string\"\n      ) {\n        setSessionId(value.sessionId);\n      }\n    },\n  });\n\n  // ... render messages; harness tool activity (Bash, Edit, Read, ...)\n  // arrives as regular tool-call parts with their results attached.\n}\n```\n\nSessions are stored on the machine that ran them (`~/.claude/projects/`), so resuming only works on the same server instance. Pass `modelOptions: { forkSession: true }` alongside `sessionId` to branch a session instead of continuing it.\n\n## Tools\n\nTwo kinds of tools flow through this adapter:\n\n1. **Built-in harness tools** (`Bash`, `Read`, `Write`, `Edit`, `Glob`, `Grep`, `WebSearch`, ...) are executed by Claude Code itself. Their activity streams back as tool-call events with results already attached, so `useChat` UIs render them with no extra wiring — but your code never executes them.\n\n2. **Your TanStack tools** are bridged *into* the harness as an in-process MCP server. Define them as usual with `toolDefinition().server()`; the model sees them as `mcp__tanstack__<name>` and the adapter strips the prefix on the way back out, so events match the names you registered.\n\n```typescript\nimport { z } from \"zod\";\nimport { chat, toolDefinition } from \"@tanstack/ai\";\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\";\n\nconst lookupTicket = toolDefinition({\n  name: \"lookup_ticket\",\n  description: \"Look up an issue ticket by id\",\n  inputSchema: z.object({ ticketId: z.string() }),\n}).server(async ({ ticketId }) => {\n  return { ticketId, status: \"open\", title: \"Crash on startup\" };\n});\n\nconst stream = chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"What's the status of ticket T-123?\" }],\n  tools: [lookupTicket],\n});\n```\n\n**Client-side and approval-gated tools are not supported.** The harness executes tools inside a live subprocess, which cannot pause across HTTP requests to wait for a browser round-trip or a human approval. Passing a tool without a server `execute()` implementation — or one marked `needsApproval` — fails fast with a descriptive error. Run those tools outside the harness with a regular provider adapter.\n\n## Structured Output\n\nPass `outputSchema` on `chat()`. Claude Code runs one harness turn, uses its native tools, and returns a typed object. The schema JSON is passed to `--json-schema` as inline JSON (the CLI rejects a file path). Tool activity and prose stream as usual. The object arrives as `structured-output.complete`, including when Claude delivers it through its built-in `StructuredOutput` tool.\n\nBy default, the adapter loads only project settings (`--setting-sources project`). Workspace projections (instructions, skills, MCP config) are project-scoped, so they apply. The host's `~/.claude` is not loaded, so a local-process run does not pick up your personal skills and hooks. A cloned repo's `.claude/settings.json` and hooks apply to the run. Set `settingSources` to change this. The adapter does not pass `--bare`, because that flag ignores a host `claude login`.\n\nOn local-process, Claude uses your host `claude login`. On Docker, pass `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` in the process env. A container has no host login.\n\n```ts\nimport { chat } from \"@tanstack/ai\"\nimport { claudeCodeText } from \"@tanstack/ai-claude-code\"\nimport { defineSandbox, withSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox\"\nimport { dockerSandbox } from \"@tanstack/ai-sandbox-docker\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nconst sandbox = defineSandbox({\n  id: \"repo-report\",\n  provider: dockerSandbox({ image: \"node:22\" }),\n})\n\nconst report = await chat({\n  adapter: claudeCodeText(\"claude-opus-4-8\"),\n  messages: [{ role: \"user\", content: \"Review this repo.\" }],\n  outputSchema: Report,\n  middleware: [withSandbox(sandbox)],\n})\n\nreport.summary\n```\n\nOn the client, pass the same schema to `useChat` and read `final`. `partial` stays empty until the end.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from \"@tanstack/ai-react\"\nimport { z } from \"zod\"\n\nconst Report = z.object({\n  summary: z.string(),\n  filesChanged: z.array(z.string()),\n})\n\nfunction ReportView() {\n  const { final, isLoading } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents(\"/api/repo-report\"),\n    outputSchema: Report,\n  })\n\n  if (isLoading) return <p>The agent is inspecting the repo.</p>\n  if (!final) return null\n  return <p>{final.summary}</p>\n}\n```\n\nIf you only need to extract JSON from a prompt and do not need a sandbox, use `@tanstack/ai-anthropic`. That path is faster.\n\nFull walkthrough, including the client: [Harness Agents](../structured-outputs/harnesses).\n\n## Limitations\n\n- **Server-only (Node).** The harness spawns a subprocess; Windows support is untested.\n- **The harness owns the agent loop.** TanStack's agent-loop strategies and per-iteration middleware don't apply inside a harness turn; `maxTurns` is the equivalent control.\n- **No sampling controls.** `temperature`-style options don't exist here.\n- **Sessions are machine-local.** Resume requires hitting the same server instance.\n- **Cold starts.** Each call spawns a harness turn; expect higher first-token latency than HTTP adapters.\n"}
